{%- comment -%}
  Stock line — prints settings.low_stock_line verbatim, nothing more.

  What used to be here: a bucket computed from `product.id | modulo: 10` that
  dealt every product one of three states (red "almost sold out" / amber
  "selling fast" / green "in stock"), mirrored in theme.js so the quick view and
  cart mini-page dealt the same card. Inventory is untracked in this theme, so
  that number described nothing — it was a stock claim generated from a product
  ID. That is a fabricated urgency signal: a dark pattern under consumer
  protection law in several jurisdictions and a Merchant Center
  misrepresentation risk. It is gone, and the amber/green tiers with it, since
  neither had a merchant-entered source at all.

  What is left is honest: if the merchant writes a stock line, it shows on every
  product it is rendered for; empty = no line anywhere. Any real per-product
  variation has to come from real inventory, which means Shopify inventory
  tracking and `variant.inventory_quantity` — not this snippet.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.scarcity_enabled and settings.low_stock_line != blank -%}
  <p class="pdp-low-stock stmt-sm"><span class="pdp-low-stock__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ settings.low_stock_line | escape }}</p>
{%- endif -%}
